"content": "Content of res://ai_skills/scripts/create_wall.gd (lines 88 to 120 of 223):
```
	# Create the opening CSG (subtraction volume)
	var opening_csg := CSGPrimitive3D.new()
	opening_csg.type = CSGPrimitive3D.BOX
	
	var local_width := width
	var local_height := height
	
	# Ensure positive dimensions
	local_width = max(local_width, 0.1)
	local_height = max(local_height, 0.1)
	
	opening_csg.transform = Transform3D.IDENTITY \\
		.with_size(Vector3(local_thickness, local_height, local_width))
	
	# Position the opening relative to wall start (in local coordinates before rotation)
	var offset_x := opening.start_position
	offset_x += config.length / 2.0  # Center around wall midpoint
	
	opening_csg.transform.origin.x = offset_x
	opening_csg.transform.origin.y = y_pos
	opening_csg.transform.origin.z = -depth / 2.0
	
	csg_root.add_child(opening_csg)

func _init() -> void:
	description = \"Creates walls with configurable dimensions, orientation, and openings (doors/windows) using CSG nodes.\"
	definition = \"\"\"\\
The CreateWallSkill creates 3D walls in a Godot scene using CSG operations.
Walls are 2.5m high by default and can be aligned with X or Z axis. The base is at Y=0.

Usage: Call create_wall() with a WallConfig object specifying:
- start_pos: World position of the wall's starting point
- direction: \"X\", \"-X\", \"Z\", or \"-Z\" for alignment direction
